the Go licence applies as stated at that URL.

3. The operating system image (Debian GNU/Linux 13 "trixie" packages)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The ISO contains unmodified Debian binary packages, including:
  Linux kernel (GPL-2.0), GNU C library (LGPL-2.1+), systemd (LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2.0+), GRUB (GPL-3.0+),
  Plymouth (GPL-2.0+), live-boot (GPL-3.0+), sway and wlroots (MIT), Chromium (BSD-3-Clause and many
  others), PipeWire/WirePlumber (MIT), NetworkManager (GPL-2.0+), BlueZ (GPL-2.0+), udisks2 (GPL-2.0+),
  polkit (LGPL-2.0+), squeekboard (GPL-3.0+), Mesa (MIT), Noto and DejaVu fonts (OFL / Bitstream Vera),
  firmware from non-free-firmware (various redistributable, non-free licences).
Each package's exact licence is in the image at /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright (kept on purpose
when the image is trimmed). The exact package versions of a build are listed in
out/<iso>.packages, written next to the ISO.

GPL / LGPL obligations when you DISTRIBUTE the ISO (giving it to others, publishing it):
you must make the corresponding source code available. Options:
  a) point recipients to the exact versions on https://snapshot.debian.org (fine for non-commercial
     distribution of unmodified Debian packages, as Debian itself documents), or
  b) build a matching source archive: run live-build with --source true --source-images tar (add it to
     EXTRA_LB_OPTIONS in tools/build-iso.sh) and distribute it alongside the ISO, or
  c) include a written offer for the source, valid for three years.
Using the ISO yourself creates no obligation.

Non-free firmware may only be redistributed under each vendor's terms (all packages in Debian's
non-free-firmware section permit redistribution as part of Debian-derived images).

